{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788126698,"nonce":"LKzDA2HNFWBdXwXtsC6JHtOp5v8=","title":"Wave 2 remediation. Depends: 2.1, 2.3 (both closed). **Gates 2.2, 2.4 (they are","message":"told to copy 2.1's exemplar) and 3.2, 3.3 (they build UX on find-rect).**\n\nClose the confirmed defects an independent review found in the wave-2 observers.\nSequencing matters more than usual here: 2.1 is the declared exemplar for 2.2\nand 2.4, and 2.3's find-rect is the query 3.2/3.3 depend on. Fix before those\nfour start, or the flaws propagate by design.\n\n\n1. **`find-rect` returns candidates that are not the nearest.**\n   `SpatialVerbs.cs:65-95`. The ring walk enumerates ORIGINS around `near`,\n   stops the instant `candidates.Count \u003e= max`, then sorts by CENTER distance.\n   But `CellRect.CenterCell = origin + (w/2,h/2)`, so center-optimal origins\n   live in a ring around `near - (w/2,h/2)`, several rings out — sorting after\n   early termination reorders the wrong set, it does not select it. The comment\n   claiming the mismatch is fixed is wrong. **Visible in 2.3's own closing\n   evidence:** `near=[114,133]` returned `[113,132]` at dist 2.2 when\n   `[112,130]` is dist 0.0. Fix: ring-walk in center space, or search to\n   `ring \u003e= bestDist + diag` before truncating.\n\n2. **Alert truncation drops by discovery order, not severity.**\n   `DigestVerb.cs:70` takes `live[0..11]`. `AlertsReadout.activeAlerts` is\n   never sorted — priority grouping happens only at draw time. A Critical alert\n   that went active most recently lands last and gets cut, so the digest can\n   show 12 Medium alerts and `more:3` while hiding\n   `Alert_ColonistNeedsRescue`. The attention model silently loses its headline.\n   The 10-alert acceptance fixture was under the cap, so this was never\n   exercised. Fix: sort by Priority descending before capping.\n\n3. **The digest's `colonists` section has no cap** (`DigestVerb.cs:86-131`),\n   while alerts, jobs and kinds all do. Spec 2.1 Invariants require \"size budget\n   enforced (truncation rules explicit)\". A 20-colonist colony is ~2.6KB of\n   colonist lines alone on a verb documented as called constantly. Note this\n   also resolves 2.1's stated Caveat 1 honestly: the caveat framed the problem\n   as unmeasured, but its own extrapolated figure (~2.1KB) is already outside\n   the \"~1-2KB\" budget. Fix: `colonists_cap` + `more`, mirroring the alert rule.\n\n4. **`map-view radius:30` is documented-legal and always fails.**\n   `SpatialVerbs.cs:31` accepts `radius \u003c= 30`; `CellRect.CenteredOn(c,30)` is\n   61x61 and `CropRenderer.cs:110` rejects `Width \u003e 60`. Every interior\n   radius-30 request errors with `bad-args`. Cap at 29 or make `MaxSide` odd.\n\n\n5. **`power` cannot answer what the spec asked.** Scope says \"generation vs\n   draw + battery days\"; the code publishes `gain_w` (the net) and `stored_wd`\n   (watt-days). Gen and draw are not separable and battery days needs draw.\n   The math that IS there is correct. 2.1's Caveat 2 (\"validated at zero only\")\n   understates: at zero, both figures are 0, which is exactly the state where\n   the missing split is invisible. Two accumulators (sum positive vs negative\n   `PowerOutput`) make it verifiable at 4.3. Rider: `nets` counts\n   `hasPowerSource`, true for a lone battery, so a battery-only grid reads as\n   powered.\n6. **Pawn glyphs collide with the item glyph space.** `Spatial.cs:225-238` uses\n   `g`/`d`/`w` for guest/tame/wild; items map to `label[0]` lowercased, so\n   `gold`-\u003e`g`, `duster`-\u003e`d`, `wood`-\u003e`w`; `Table` and `Tree` are both `T`.\n   The legend then merges them: `legend[\"d\"] = \"tame animal | duster (Muffalo)\"`.\n   With a 32-mod catalog collisions are the common case. Reserve a disjoint\n   band for pawns before 3.2/3.3 read these crops.\n7. **The `designations` layer renders under `things`** (`Spatial.cs:186`), but\n   almost every designation is ON a thing. Designate a wall for deconstruction\n   and `--layers terrain,things,designations` shows `#` and no `*`. Designations\n   are an overlay; they should outrank things.\n\n- `threats.kinds` iterates a Dictionary and takes the first 3 in hash order,\n  not \"top-3\" as the resolution comment promises — unstable across runs, which\n  matters for rwtest's stable-field-name contract. Sort by count descending.\n- A fully off-map rect returns `ok:true` with a 0-wide crop and an off-map\n  origin; `bad-args` is the honest answer. (2.3's edge acceptance used only\n  overlapping rects.)\n- `find-rect` gives up silently at `ExamineCap`/ring 80; empty candidates is\n  ambiguous between \"none nearby\" and \"stopped looking\". Add `capped` /\n  `searched_radius` — the spec's invariant is candidates AND REASONS.\n- `nearest {def:\"MinifiedThing\"}` makes `ListerThings` emit a red error from\n  agent-supplied args, against the zero-red-errors invariant.\n- `job` swallows every exception to null, indistinguishable from \"no job\" and\n  not journaled. With 32 mods this hides the class of failure that invariant\n  exists to surface.\n- Resource counts are stockpile-only (`ResourceCounter` walks haul destinations,\n  so unzoned goods read zero). Documented in a git-bug comment and nowhere a\n  later spec will look; a wave-3 build verb gating on `steel` will refuse on a\n  colony with 5000 steel on the ground. Put it in the field docs.\n- `since` is narrowed to `int` through `VerbRegistry`; journal seq is `long`.\n\n`DigestVerb.cs:109` calls `Room.Role` per colonist per digest. That is a lazy\nfull room analysis — every RoomStatDef and RoomRoleDef worker, cell and content\nwalks — and `statsAndRoleDirty` is set from six sites, so ordinary hauling makes\nthis recompute constantly. Idempotent and RNG-free, so not a correctness defect,\nbut it is a cost defect sitting in the file that is explicitly the exemplar,\nand its only loud mutation comment is about `FreeColonistsSpawned`. The same\nhazard IS commented at `SpatialVerbs.cs:258` for `room-at`. Comment it here, and\nadd `DangerWatcher.DangerRating` to the exemplar's warning list — it rebuilds\n`FreeColonistsSpawned` internally, so 2.2/2.4 copying the pattern could call it\ninside a `FreeColonistsSpawned` loop and get a live bug.\n\n- `find-rect` on a fixture where the center-optimal origin is 3+ rings out\n  returns it first; the 2.3 closing-evidence case now returns `[112,130]`.\n- With 15 active alerts including one Critical added last, the digest lists the\n  Critical and truncates a Medium.\n- A 20-colonist fixture keeps the digest inside budget with an explicit `more`.\n- `map-view {radius:30}` succeeds.\n- Power reports gen and draw separately, verified against the in-game power tab\n  on a colony with a generator, a battery and a load.","files":null}]}